# sriq: a SYMMETRIC role. A has an r-successor in B, and B sends its r-successors
# into C; r is symmetric, so A, being one of them, is a C.
# Expect: A ⊑ C.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty , owl:SymmetricProperty .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] .
:B rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:allValuesFrom :C ] .
